EVALUATION.md §1, CODEGEN.md §5.6 (gen/go dependentUnionFormat, gen/cpp unionDependent): neither data loader reads a literal union over a dependent type, so such a field of a class it decodes is DependentType at the field, in both loaders.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A kind.
enum K { one, two }

/// A payload.
type P(k: K) = match k { one => String, two => String }

/// A thing.
record Thing {
  /// Its kind.
  k: K
  /// Its payload, or none.
  u: P(k) | "none"
}

/// The things.
let things: table Thing = {
  a { k: one, u: "x" }
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: data }
emit cpp { out: "@features/ac", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- a.things.json --
{"a": {"k": "one", "u": "x"}}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:14:3
  emit cpp in data mode cannot generate a dependent type

error[E8019]  a/a.canon:14:3
  emit go in data mode cannot generate a dependent type

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
